Chris Bernard.

00:12:46.990 --> 00:12:54.430
>> Good evening, Chris Bernard, address is 58 Merritt Valley Road, and I am speaking as a member of the board of education.

00:12:54.910 --> 00:12:57.550
I support the proposed AES budget,

00:12:57.790 --> 00:13:02.605
not only because of the hard work of the school administration and my fellow board of education members,

00:13:02.845 --> 00:13:04.925
but because it's a prudent course of action.

00:13:05.485 --> 00:13:10.445
For a bit of background on myself, I hold a doctor of education degree in educational leadership.

00:13:11.245 --> 00:13:13.485
Was on how ideology

00:13:13.290 --> 00:13:16.570
and pedagogy impact the adoption of technology in the classroom.

00:13:17.050 --> 00:13:21.050
While my dissertation was centered on technology use, it was of course important to understand

00:13:21.290 --> 00:13:22.650
the historical

00:13:22.810 --> 00:13:23.450
past

00:13:23.770 --> 00:13:24.810
significance

00:13:24.810 --> 00:13:26.010
of pedagogy,

00:13:26.010 --> 00:13:27.450
something that we have all experienced.

00:13:28.695 --> 00:13:31.415
As we discussed the proposed Board of Education budget,

00:13:31.575 --> 00:13:36.535
one item I would like everyone to keep in mind is the ever changing role of education in society.

00:13:37.015 --> 00:13:40.455
Many of us were educated for a very different world than what we live in now.

00:13:41.030 --> 00:13:44.710
As part of the industrial revolution, the eighteenth and nineteenth centuries,

00:13:44.870 --> 00:13:57.845
many of us were educated in some very formalized and standardized ways that continue to this day, with the primary goal of the education system to be to be creating a standardized worker for factories and labor.

00:13:58.805 --> 00:14:03.045
This standardized approach to education led to larger class sizes and more efficiencies.

00:14:03.365 --> 00:14:09.690
But as a targeted the average student, it often failed to serve the vast majority of students in the best way possible.

00:14:10.090 --> 00:14:14.090
Those students who did not fit the mold simply never reached their potential.

00:14:14.410 --> 00:14:18.090
This, of course, includes students both above and below the average.

00:14:19.015 --> 00:14:23.495
As our nation has changed from an industrial economy to a service and knowledge based economy,

00:14:23.655 --> 00:14:24.935
so must our education.

00:14:25.255 --> 00:14:32.070
To do so means we must change how we teach and interact with students, moving from the sage on stage to the guide on the side,

00:14:32.390 --> 00:14:34.790
especially in the more formative years of schooling.

00:14:35.030 --> 00:14:38.870
This means increased interaction with students leading to smaller class sizes.

00:14:39.350 --> 00:15:03.550
We have seen firsthand the impact of not investing in our future. We hear regularly about the ever increasing cost to repair roads and infrastructure that not been maintained over the years. Roads and buildings can be repaired. Our children cannot. Same as Dan said, by the way, we did not coordinate that at all. I understand the concern and recognize challenge trying to meet the needs of all members of our community, a daunting task before the board finance, board selectman and community as a whole,

00:15:03.950 --> 00:15:07.390
and look forward to working together and meeting the needs of all. Thanks.

