and actually to manage the process. And we're fortunate to have somebody who's gone through a software transition before

00:53:05.770 --> 00:53:14.315
kind of in a leadership role. So again, that's another one of those things I'm happy to punt to somebody that's more qualified than me.

00:53:17.755 --> 00:53:22.075
>> If we have no further questions on that item

00:53:21.790 --> 00:53:29.310
7D is the audit status and I think that's also something we were kind of, I don't know if we have any updates but that's really kind of

00:53:30.030 --> 00:53:33.150
something that's going to be the finance director's

00:53:33.150 --> 00:53:38.375
>> job to kind of move along. Right? Well, so right now the audit is underway.

00:53:39.895 --> 00:53:42.855
We have basically the town

00:53:42.855 --> 00:53:43.655
has

00:53:43.895 --> 00:53:45.175
subcontracted

00:53:45.175 --> 00:53:47.255
with the AES,

00:53:47.255 --> 00:53:49.015
the old AES business

00:53:49.015 --> 00:53:51.070
manager Laura to

00:53:51.070 --> 00:53:52.350
give us a hand.

00:53:53.390 --> 00:53:54.430
And we

00:53:56.110 --> 00:53:58.670
gave the information that we had

00:53:58.990 --> 00:53:59.710
to

00:53:59.790 --> 00:54:01.070
the auditor

00:54:01.470 --> 00:54:05.295
and Mike has sent us back a, you know, request

00:54:05.295 --> 00:54:08.255
for a series of other pieces of information,

00:54:09.135 --> 00:54:15.615
both a lot of the stuff with their audit. You know, they asked us to pull, you know, 30 or 35 different

00:54:16.895 --> 00:54:24.760
items that we purchased or bid or something like that and grabbed all the supporting detail to make sure we're doing it per our policies.

00:54:25.560 --> 00:54:30.680
So we're in the process right now of preparing that to send back to them.

00:54:31.555 --> 00:54:36.115
It looks like we have about 85 or 90% of the stuff we need

00:54:36.355 --> 00:54:38.755
to complete the audit at this point.

