Okay,

00:55:24.510 --> 00:55:29.475
let's move on to new business. The moment you've all been waiting for. Obviously

00:55:30.995 --> 00:55:32.035
we're gonna

00:55:33.875 --> 00:55:35.475
have our presentation.

00:55:35.715 --> 00:55:41.235
Item 8A is the presentation of 2021 and 2022 Andover Elementary School proposed budget.

00:55:42.080 --> 00:55:43.040
Superintendent

00:55:43.040 --> 00:55:45.840
Valerie Bruno is going to be making the presentation.

00:55:45.920 --> 00:55:49.200
I want to thank you all for coming out tonight and

00:55:50.000 --> 00:55:52.080
helping us along here.

00:55:52.240 --> 00:55:58.355
And again, congratulations on keeping the students in school. Know that's a tough thing to do over the last

00:56:00.435 --> 00:56:03.715
eight months. It's been a last year really. It's been a tough one.

00:56:05.075 --> 00:56:05.875
Congratulations

00:56:05.875 --> 00:56:08.115
on that. So I'll turn it over to you, Valerie.

00:56:09.570 --> 00:56:10.210
>> Thanks.

00:56:10.530 --> 00:56:11.730
So it has been a

00:56:12.210 --> 00:56:15.090
tough go of things. And I know that

00:56:15.410 --> 00:56:23.730
Joanne Hebert said, we really don't want to get too emotional when we do things. Before I begin though, do want one just one minute of emotion,

00:56:24.235 --> 00:56:32.875
because we are 32 adults that are on these screens right now. And all I want you to do is think about the last twelve months.

00:56:33.035 --> 00:56:37.755
And if there was even one time in the last twelve months that you felt overwhelmed

00:56:37.800 --> 00:56:39.000
by the pandemic

00:56:39.160 --> 00:56:42.440
and wanted someone to call and wanted someone to talk to.

00:56:42.760 --> 00:56:48.840
School's been open now since the start of the school year and these kids are still going through this. And so this budget

00:56:49.000 --> 00:56:52.040
is very different because as the superintendent,

00:56:52.120 --> 00:56:53.160
I have to look at finances,

00:56:53.735 --> 00:56:58.055
but I have to also look and make sure that those needs of our kids

00:56:58.215 --> 00:57:02.935
are going to be met in this upcoming school year. So that's very important.

00:57:03.095 --> 00:57:08.855
And I'm sure every one of us, all 32 of us could say, yep, there was that one day I just cried for no reason.

00:57:09.600 --> 00:57:17.040
So I want everyone to keep that one emotion in mind when we consider what we potentially need going forward.

00:57:17.760 --> 00:57:20.640
So with that, I'm going to see if I can share my screen here.

00:57:23.665 --> 00:57:25.505
And does she also have to do that?

00:57:25.905 --> 00:57:27.105
I think so.

00:57:27.585 --> 00:57:28.385
Okay.

00:57:29.185 --> 00:57:30.225
There you go.

00:57:30.545 --> 00:57:33.425
>> Okay. Can everybody see this? Yeah. Yes?

00:57:33.900 --> 00:57:34.700
I

00:57:35.020 --> 00:57:37.820
can't really see any of you guys now. It's fine.

00:57:38.300 --> 00:57:39.500
Thank you so much.

00:57:40.220 --> 00:57:56.485
So yes, this is the twenty twenty one-twenty two budget for the upcoming school year. I'm going to actually close out my corner here so that I can't see anybody because otherwise I can't see the whole screen. And I know Mark, you and the rest of the board are in receipt of

00:57:57.285 --> 00:57:58.565
Chairwoman Shannon

00:57:58.645 --> 00:58:05.520
her transmittal letter that came with this as well. So as we go through here, I'm going to kind of fast forward through a few

00:58:06.080 --> 00:58:07.600
of these things that

00:58:07.840 --> 00:58:11.440
we'll get to as we get there. But we have a timeline here

00:58:12.000 --> 00:58:21.195
and we have already approved and adopted on the board of ed side. What we believe to be a good fiscally responsible

00:58:21.595 --> 00:58:23.995
budget proposal. We did that in January.

00:58:24.075 --> 00:58:29.435
So here we are with the board of finance and this is what we'll see through all the way until June,

00:58:29.675 --> 00:58:31.035
when budget is approved.

00:58:33.380 --> 00:58:39.620
I included the mission and the vision because I want people to see the mission statement and the vision statement

00:58:39.940 --> 00:58:42.020
of the school and the board,

00:58:42.180 --> 00:58:54.295
because we're looking to make sure that we have a strong curriculum that's challenging and creative for all in a safe environment. Those words take on a new meeting this year when we talk about safe environment

00:58:54.375 --> 00:58:55.575
amidst COVID.

00:58:55.815 --> 00:59:00.615
We want to make sure we nurture the kids. We want to make sure that they have values of responsibility,

00:59:00.615 --> 00:59:02.295
respectfulness, and a desire of learning.

00:59:02.990 --> 00:59:04.910
We look at the vision statement.

00:59:04.910 --> 00:59:08.110
We want to make sure again that we have a safe educational

00:59:08.110 --> 00:59:08.910
environment,

00:59:08.910 --> 00:59:10.590
not just a physical environment

00:59:10.830 --> 00:59:14.270
that establishes a foundation for students to become creative,

00:59:14.270 --> 00:59:15.870
moral and compassionate people.

00:59:16.985 --> 00:59:24.825
So this vision and mission statement hasn't changed. We move forward to the next school year with this same thing in mind. That's why we do this.

00:59:26.585 --> 00:59:35.470
Now the who we do it for. I know that this slide has been a bone of contention. I know Mr. Foran had spoken about this. Dan had spoken about this.

00:59:35.870 --> 00:59:48.105
I know it's very difficult for some people who are not currently in the school right now to understand why we have the three kindergarten classes. And yes, that is absolutely the elephant in the room.

00:59:49.465 --> 00:59:50.185
Understand

00:59:50.265 --> 00:59:52.585
that we are not adding staff.

00:59:53.065 --> 01:00:00.710
As a matter of fact, when we look at the number of classrooms you can see there it's 14. It's remained 14 from the 2018

01:00:00.710 --> 01:00:03.750
school year all the way through till the end of twenty two.

01:00:04.710 --> 01:00:14.105
We are not adding a classroom. We are not adding any teachers. What we're doing is we are taking the same number of classrooms and although we have

01:00:14.345 --> 01:00:16.185
a teacher that is retiring

01:00:16.505 --> 01:00:19.705
this year, we are eliminating a paraprofessional

01:00:19.705 --> 01:00:20.505
position

01:00:20.745 --> 01:00:25.225
and taking that person who was working with our preschoolers

01:00:24.620 --> 01:00:26.700
who is a teacher certified

01:00:26.940 --> 01:00:29.660
and moving her to that third kindergarten class.

01:00:29.740 --> 01:00:34.940
So it is still quite a reduction already on our part. It's a reduction of one position,

01:00:35.100 --> 01:00:36.700
which is a paraprofessional position,

01:00:37.285 --> 01:00:43.205
and a reduction from a teacher who's at the top of the step to a teacher who will be at the beginning

01:00:43.365 --> 01:00:44.725
of the ladder.

01:00:45.445 --> 01:00:50.325
And I do agree with naysayers that in any other year, we would consider

01:00:50.590 --> 01:00:54.590
making those class sizes in kindergarten and grade three larger.

01:00:55.230 --> 01:01:03.630
But it is my opinion and my professional opinion that in doing so we could in the long run wind up with extensive

01:01:03.630 --> 01:01:06.030
costs related to not addressing

01:01:06.185 --> 01:01:12.185
the learning gap potential needs of these kids. And I have explained publicly once before

01:01:12.345 --> 01:01:17.865
that we already know beyond a shadow of a doubt that those 30 kindergarten

01:01:17.865 --> 01:01:18.585
kids

01:01:19.145 --> 01:01:21.065
include eight kids that are coming in

01:01:21.800 --> 01:01:24.200
that we know have not been in preschool

01:01:24.520 --> 01:01:26.600
through the whole pandemic.

01:01:27.720 --> 01:01:31.640
We know also that we have three existing

01:01:33.160 --> 01:01:36.040
preschoolers that are set to move up to kindergarten

01:01:36.595 --> 01:01:37.395
that

01:01:37.475 --> 01:01:39.155
have significant needs

01:01:39.635 --> 01:01:41.875
and they have individual paraprofessional

01:01:41.875 --> 01:01:43.235
needs. And so

01:01:43.715 --> 01:01:49.875
taking those 30 kids and placing them fifteen and fifteen in a classroom is not advantageous.

01:01:49.875 --> 01:02:01.060
I consider this a COVID related expense for us to keep the current staff instead of cutting it. And again, we're not adding any staff members. What we're doing is keeping the existing

01:02:01.140 --> 01:02:05.220
staff members there. You'll notice those top three classes are getting bigger.

01:02:05.745 --> 01:02:08.305
And once we get through this pandemic,

01:02:08.785 --> 01:02:16.145
then we will see those classes. I'm not opposed to larger class sizes in any other year. That's not something that

01:02:16.785 --> 01:02:23.570
I have a problem with. I think that what we will see in the coming years is grades three, two, and one

01:02:23.730 --> 01:02:24.530
significantly

01:02:24.530 --> 01:02:26.690
increasing the class sizes

01:02:27.250 --> 01:02:28.370
as the years

01:02:28.690 --> 01:02:29.650
go on here.

01:02:30.450 --> 01:02:30.930
Okay.

01:02:32.225 --> 01:02:35.345
So what's changed? Well, we said COVID-nineteen

01:02:35.345 --> 01:02:38.945
pandemic from last year to this year. That's really shifted

01:02:39.265 --> 01:02:48.440
the world to distance learning. So there have been distance learning expenses and there have been some changes that need to take place within the building to accommodate.

01:02:48.600 --> 01:02:51.560
We're very proud of the fact that at the beginning of the year,

01:02:51.880 --> 01:02:52.920
we had

01:02:53.000 --> 01:02:58.600
about nineteen percent of the kids that originally started on distance learning.

01:02:59.160 --> 01:03:06.675
Last week, we were down to six percent. And as of next week, we will be down to almost able to count on one hand

01:03:06.835 --> 01:03:13.635
the number of kids. We need two hands, but we're getting there. The number of students that have returned to school.

01:03:14.195 --> 01:03:15.955
So that's fantastic.

01:03:16.220 --> 01:03:33.355
However, we will need to make sure that we're always ready on a moment's notice to go back to distance learning with sickness, with flu, with pandemic, with anything. We'll have to be ready for that in the future. And that's just not something that we had to plan for prior to this year. Obviously, a new superintendent.

01:03:34.315 --> 01:03:37.355
We had reopening plans that needed to be solidified.

01:03:37.355 --> 01:03:39.275
We had teacher contracts,

01:03:39.275 --> 01:03:42.875
which we only get every four years. And unfortunately for the budget,

01:03:43.035 --> 01:03:44.875
this happens to be one of those years.

01:03:46.030 --> 01:03:48.510
Our enrollment has remained stagnant.

01:03:48.510 --> 01:03:55.870
We're right about the same that we've been for the past few years, give or take a couple of kids. No dramatic huge changes there.

01:03:57.230 --> 01:03:58.670
We signed a teacher

01:03:58.910 --> 01:03:59.790
MOA,

01:04:00.030 --> 01:04:01.070
which was an agreement,

01:04:01.625 --> 01:04:04.345
a memorandum of agreement or understanding

01:04:04.425 --> 01:04:09.145
as to what the work conditions would be. And that went very well. And the teachers

01:04:09.305 --> 01:04:12.345
were ready to jump right into action at the beginning of the year.

01:04:12.985 --> 01:04:19.110
We have a non cert contract that's just moments away or days away from being finished.

01:04:19.110 --> 01:04:29.415
And so we have to consider the costs associated with that in this budget as well. And as Eric had mentioned earlier, we have the business offices merging. And on our end,

01:04:29.575 --> 01:04:37.015
although we're sharing it, we had a part time business manager before. So there will be some difference in cost for us there as well.

01:04:38.055 --> 01:04:43.930
And then we do have new requirements, recommendations as well as mandates for safety and health that will need to be implemented.

01:04:44.250 --> 01:04:47.370
If they've already been implemented, they'll need to be maintained.

01:04:48.250 --> 01:04:51.690
So how will we do this within AES logistically?

01:04:51.690 --> 01:04:53.210
Well, in terms of staffing,

01:04:53.450 --> 01:04:54.795
yes, we

01:04:55.035 --> 01:05:00.315
can't get rid of any staff members that are currently here, but we're also not asking for any new staff.

01:05:00.955 --> 01:05:07.355
And I know there are other towns that do have to, due to the number of students that they have on distance learning,

01:05:07.760 --> 01:05:10.480
they've had no choice but to bring in other bodies.

01:05:11.120 --> 01:05:12.240
And because

01:05:12.480 --> 01:05:14.720
our dedicated staff has been here

01:05:16.240 --> 01:05:17.200
the whole time,

01:05:17.520 --> 01:05:21.760
we've been very lucky that we don't have a need to ask the taxpayers

01:05:22.085 --> 01:05:28.165
to offer us more staff for that for next year because we're doing pretty well with the distance learning

01:05:28.405 --> 01:05:30.005
being able to staff that.

01:05:31.205 --> 01:05:34.645
We'll have the same number of classrooms next year. Again, we're not adding any more.

01:05:36.230 --> 01:05:43.910
And we'll have to continue with comparable classroom spending and just not add any other initiatives. So when you look at this budget, you won't see

01:05:44.150 --> 01:05:46.950
any new initiatives, any new curriculum,

01:05:47.190 --> 01:05:49.350
any new large scale supplies.

01:05:49.350 --> 01:05:53.935
We've had to just say that's got to be on hold for now. We're just going to have to

01:05:54.335 --> 01:06:01.535
steer the ship with the good solid curriculum that we currently have and not look for any more innovative things.

01:06:02.895 --> 01:06:19.105
We did speak with the teachers union and say, okay, it's budget season. What do you guys need next year? And they said, just need to make sure that we maintain a level of professional development so that we can continue to be ready at all times for distance learning. And we can

01:06:19.425 --> 01:06:26.945
go with the times and make sure that we're switching over from all of the consumables that we might use to integrating

01:06:26.945 --> 01:06:28.545
some more technology.

01:06:28.625 --> 01:06:33.110
I know a lot of people think, you have a computer, there's no costs associated with technology,

01:06:33.110 --> 01:06:36.950
which there are because there's licenses to be able to use certain tech.

01:06:37.510 --> 01:06:43.830
So how will we do this? I'm going to take a quick peek as we go through by object area in hopes of being able to

01:06:44.390 --> 01:06:58.455
assist all of the members of the board as well as the town that are on tonight to understand. Valerie, can you explain what's meant by object? I don't know that that's clear to everybody. It's going be confusing. Yep. So as we go through, you'll see that

01:06:58.695 --> 01:07:00.535
there are categories

01:07:01.180 --> 01:07:01.980
of

01:07:02.540 --> 01:07:09.340
costs and they're all when they're all related to one another, they all fall under one sub number. So as we go through,

01:07:10.060 --> 01:07:11.500
I will point those out.

01:07:11.820 --> 01:07:13.900
So I'm going to start with

01:07:14.405 --> 01:07:15.125
what

01:07:15.365 --> 01:07:17.445
revenue we have coming in besides

01:07:17.685 --> 01:07:20.885
the money from the town. I'll look at preschool first.

01:07:21.925 --> 01:07:22.725
And again,

01:07:22.965 --> 01:07:28.325
you'll have you guys will have to if you need me to stop you'll have to shout out because I can't see any of you while I'm sharing my screen.

01:07:29.350 --> 01:07:36.070
So we do have for preschool, we have money that comes in from the school readiness grant about $100,000

01:07:36.150 --> 01:07:38.390
And that's used to pay some salaries

01:07:38.710 --> 01:07:39.830
and PD.

01:07:40.230 --> 01:07:46.685
We have money that comes in from smart start grant, and that goes toward our second pair professional salary there.

01:07:47.885 --> 01:07:59.130
And other grant requirements. I know at one point there was some question about some of the things that we do provide in the program. At one point, I know a parent did ask about things like snacks and things like

01:07:59.850 --> 01:08:00.650
supplies.

01:08:01.450 --> 01:08:03.530
Because we're the beneficiaries

01:08:03.610 --> 01:08:06.170
of these revenue sources,

01:08:06.410 --> 01:08:07.690
there are specific guidelines.

01:08:08.105 --> 01:08:30.590
For example, you will see orders that come in of toothpastes and toothbrushes, and people say you're spending your money on toothpaste. Well, we have to because part of the curriculum is to make sure that with hygiene that the kids brush their teeth. We don't pay for that out of our taxpayer dollars. That comes out of the grant. But to get the grant, you have to make sure that you follow suit. The same thing with the snacks. They give you guidelines and things like that.

01:08:31.390 --> 01:08:35.790
In the quality enhancement grant is only for professional development for

01:08:36.350 --> 01:08:37.550
the preschool program.

01:08:38.325 --> 01:08:44.725
So when we look, we bring in tuition costs that on a normal year, we can usually expect to be about 90,000.

01:08:44.725 --> 01:08:46.245
Now, I will say

01:08:46.885 --> 01:08:49.205
that last year with COVID,

01:08:49.205 --> 01:08:49.765
excuse me,

01:08:51.620 --> 01:08:55.540
with COVID there was a time period where we weren't bringing in the same revenue.

01:08:56.180 --> 01:09:00.900
And so that can fluctuate depending on what occurs, the number of children go up or down.

01:09:01.300 --> 01:09:03.140
So 90 is the average there.

01:09:03.825 --> 01:09:05.185
So when we look,

01:09:05.505 --> 01:09:09.825
it is self sufficient with the exception of the benefits to the employees.

01:09:10.145 --> 01:09:14.145
And I know that a lot of other towns, you look at Hebron, if you look at Marlborough,

01:09:14.145 --> 01:09:22.330
the benefits are not separated out. They're right in the rest of their budget so that people don't realize that. But we are very transparently saying yes,

01:09:22.650 --> 01:09:28.250
that is the only cost. The only cost is the benefits to the employees that are that work in that program.

01:09:29.475 --> 01:09:35.795
